---
title: Creamy Pesto Pasta with Asparagus & Butter Beans
portions: 4
category: Pasta
source: "https://www.cinnamonsnail.com/vegan-pesto-pasta/"
---

## Pesto

[Toast] Lightly toast the @pine-nuts{80 g} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat, ~{3 min}.

[Blend] Place the @basil{90 g}, the @lemon-juice{15 ml}, the @olive-oil{80 ml}, the toasted @pine-nuts{}, the @garlic{3 g}(1 clove), the @nutritional-yeast{5 g} and the @water{60 ml} in a #food processor{}. Blend until smooth, scraping down the sides. Set aside.

## Pasta

[Boil] Bring a large #pot{} of water to a rolling boil over high heat. Add the @salt{8 g} and the @pasta{400 g}(calamarata). Cook according to package timing, stirring occasionally. Reserve the pasta cooking @water{120 ml}, then drain.

[Sauté] Heat the @olive-oil{20 ml} in a large #pan{} or Dutch oven over medium heat. Add the sliced @garlic{6 g}(2 cloves) and the @asparagus{150 g}(tips) and sauté until softened without darkening, ~{60 s}.

[Toss] Add the drained @butter-beans{240 g}, the cooked pasta and the pesto to the #pan{}. Toss continuously until evenly coated, loosening with reserved cooking water a few tablespoons at a time.

## Serve

[Serve] Divide into bowls and finish with extra @basil{}, chopped @parsley{} and vegan parmesan.
